 # Ray-Splat/Gaussian Intersection
 
-Also called: Ray-Gaussian Intersection, Ray-Quadric Intersection
 
 ## Overview
-This family defines the geometric intersection between a camera ray and 3D Gaussian splats, which are ellipsoidal primitives used in novel view synthesis. It solves the problem of accurately determining which splats contribute to a pixel and at what depth, enabling alpha blending and depth-based operations. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by handling the specific quadratic nature of Gaussian density fields, supporting both exact ellipsoid intersection and numerical stabilization for degenerate cases, unlike [Sphere Intersection](1620-sphere-intersection.md) which assumes constant radius or [Ray-Triangle Intersection](11312-ray-triangle-intersection.md) which handles planar surfaces.
+This family defines the geometric intersection between a camera ray and 3D Gaussian splats, which are ellipsoidal primitives used in novel view synthesis [G]. It solves the problem of accurately determining which splats contribute to a pixel and at what depth, enabling alpha blending and depth-based operations [G]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by handling the specific quadratic nature of Gaussian density fields, supporting both exact ellipsoid intersection and numerical stabilization for degenerate cases, unlike [Sphere Intersection](1620-sphere-intersection.md) which assumes constant radius or [Ray-Triangle Intersection](11312-ray-triangle-intersection.md) which handles planar surfaces [G].
 
